  "id": "COMPOUND:9917 - PROTEIN:5792",
  "verbalization": "Osugacestat is implicated in the regulation of RWLeu4 through a series of molecular interactions involving T-cell surface glycoprotein CD3. The evidence suggests that Osugacestat acts as a target for multiple compounds, including Phyllofolactones F and Lup-20(29)-en-3-ol, which in turn target RWLeu4. These findings indicate a potential pathway where Osugacestat influences the activity of CD3, which is a critical component of the T-cell receptor complex. The presence of multiple targets, each with a direct link to RWLeu4, suggests a complex regulatory mechanism that may involve the modulation of T-cell signaling pathways. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of CD3 in the context of T-cell function and its potential role in the regulation of RWLeu4. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Osugacestat and RWLeu4, emphasizing the role of CD3 in this relationship.",
